<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Mohammed Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1748</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali Mohammed Khan was the founder of Rohilla power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilkhand">Rohilkhand</a>, the region east of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>. Adopted son of the Afghan chief Daud Khan, he built a following of Rohilla soldiers from the 1720s, made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aonla">Aonla</a> his capital and won recognition from the Mughal emperor. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faizullah-khan">Faizullah Khan</a> later founded the princely state of Rampur.</p></div>
